@page "/localization"

<PageTitle>Localization</PageTitle>
<h1>Localization</h1>
<p>Two mechanisms translate this form's messages: FluentValidation translates its own default messages by the current UI culture, and the one custom message comes from a pair of resource (resx) files. Switch the language and the messages, the date and the number all follow.</p>

<TeachingPanel CodeFiles="@(new[] { "LocalizedProfile.cs", "CultureBootstrap.cs", "Localization.razor", "Localization.razor.cs" })">
    <TryIt>
        <p>Before the steps, check the <strong>Messages and formats</strong> picker under <strong>Language</strong>, which keeps your last pick. If it does not show <strong>English (Australia)</strong>, pick that first; the page reloads.</p>
        <ol>
            <li>Look at the line under the form.<div class="teaching__result"><span class="teaching__label">You see:</span> today's date written out in English, and the number <code>1,234.56</code>.</div></li>
            <li>Click <strong>Submit</strong> with both boxes empty.<div class="teaching__result"><span class="teaching__label">You see:</span> "'Full Name' must not be empty." under <strong>Full Name</strong> and "Age must be a whole number between 18 and 130" under <strong>Age</strong>.</div><div class="teaching__why"><span class="teaching__label">Why:</span> <strong>Age</strong>'s range check fails an empty box, though it is not a required rule.</div></li>
            <li>Pick <strong>Deutsch (Deutschland)</strong> in the picker.<div class="teaching__result"><span class="teaching__label">You see:</span> the page reloads with empty boxes, and the line under the form shows the date in German and the number as <code>1.234,56</code>.</div><div class="teaching__why"><span class="teaching__label">Why:</span> WebAssembly fixes the culture at startup, so the page stores your pick and reloads.</div></li>
            <li>Click <strong>Submit</strong> with both boxes empty again.<div class="teaching__result"><span class="teaching__label">You see:</span> "'Full Name' darf nicht leer sein." and "Das Alter muss eine ganze Zahl zwischen 18 und 130 sein".</div><div class="teaching__why"><span class="teaching__label">Why:</span> FluentValidation translates its messages; display names like 'Full Name' are a separate job.</div></li>
            <li>Type <code>30</code> into <strong>Age</strong> and press Tab.<div class="teaching__result"><span class="teaching__label">You see:</span> the message under <strong>Age</strong> clears.</div></li>
            <li>Replace <strong>Age</strong> with <code>12</code> and press Tab.<div class="teaching__result"><span class="teaching__label">You see:</span> "Das Alter muss eine ganze Zahl zwischen 18 und 130 sein" again.</div></li>
            <li>Pick <strong>English (Australia)</strong> in the picker.<div class="teaching__result"><span class="teaching__label">You see:</span> the page reloads, and the line under the form shows English formats again.</div></li>
        </ol>
    </TryIt>
    <Rules>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Full Name</strong>: required.</li>
            <li><strong>Age</strong>: a whole number from 18 to 130.</li>
        </ul>
    </Rules>
    <HowItWorks>
        <p><strong>Full Name</strong>'s rule has no <code>WithMessage</code>, so it keeps FluentValidation's default message. FluentValidation ships translations of its default messages and picks one by <code>CultureInfo.CurrentUICulture</code>, so a rule that keeps the default message is translated for free.</p>
        <p><strong>Age</strong>'s message is the app's own, so it comes from a resource pair: <code>ValidationMessages.resx</code> (English) and <code>ValidationMessages.de.resx</code> (German). The rule passes it as a message factory (a function), so the lookup happens each time the rule runs and always matches the culture in force.</p>
        <p>The page places a <code>FormidableRequiredIndicator</code> (the component that draws the mark) beside <strong>Full Name</strong> only. <strong>Age</strong> has no required rule (<code>NotEmpty()</code> or <code>NotNull()</code>), only a range check written with <code>Must</code>, so a <code>FormidableRequiredIndicator</code> placed beside it would draw nothing. An empty box still fails the range check.</p>
        <p>WebAssembly fixes the culture at startup, so switching reloads the app. The page stores your pick in the browser under <code>formidable.culture</code>, and <code>Program.cs</code> applies it before the app starts. That is also when the browser downloads the German resource assembly, once German is picked. That plumbing is the app's own (<code>CultureBootstrap</code>, under <strong>Show the code</strong>); Formidable ships none of it.</p>
        <p>FluentValidation's translated messages still name the field in English ('Full Name' darf nicht leer sein.). Translating display names is a separate job (with <code>WithName</code>, for example), which this page leaves out.</p>
        <p>The line under the form writes today's date in full and a number under the culture in force. The page's own text, this panel included, stays English whatever you pick; only the form's messages and that line follow the culture.</p>
    </HowItWorks>
    <Demo>
        <fieldset class="culture">
            <legend>Language</legend>
            <label>Messages and formats
                <select value="@Culture" @onchange="SwitchCulture">
                    <option value="en-AU">English (Australia)</option>
                    <option value="de-DE">Deutsch (Deutschland)</option>
                </select>
            </label>
        </fieldset>

        <FormidableForm Model="_profile" OnValidSubmit="HandleValid">
            <div class="summary-slot">
                <FormidableSummary />
            </div>

            <div class="field"><label>Full Name <FormidableRequiredIndicator For="() => _profile.FullName" /> <FormidableInputText @bind-Value="_profile.FullName" /></label>
                <FormidableFieldMessage For="() => _profile.FullName" /></div>
            <div class="field"><label>Age <FormidableInputText @bind-Value="_profile.Age" /></label>
                <FormidableFieldMessage For="() => _profile.Age" /></div>

            <div class="actions"><button type="submit">Submit</button></div>
        </FormidableForm>

        <p><small>Culture-sensitive formatting under @Culture: today is @DateTime.Today.ToString("D"), and a number reads @(1234.56.ToString("N2")).</small></p>
        <p role="status">@_status</p>
    </Demo>
</TeachingPanel>
